# promise: #632
# Each page of Arc's theme presets places a second and third colour its own way (Arc 1.174, measured
# offline 20 Nov 2026): a Brand, Pastel, Drab or Greyscale swatch is one colour, and + takes it across
# the wheel (`complimentary`: 180°, then 150° and 210°, in Display P3); a page-2 swatch is three
# colours 40° either side (`analogous`). − puts the rest back where the wheel puts that many. Before,
# every + went 40° on in sRGB and page 2 gave two colours.
budget rss=700 stalls50=10
cra://debug?windowSize=1280x900
wait 1
cra://debug?themeEditor=1
wait 1
# Brand red: + gives Arc's cyan, a second + splits it into Arc's green and blue, − puts the cyan back.
cra://debug?themeEditor=swatch:03
expect-log theme editor pad 1: wheel=complimentary key=#F25E6B$
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
expect-log theme editor pad 2: wheel=complimentary key=#F25E6B,#0[01]E4DB$
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
expect-log theme editor pad 3: wheel=complimentary key=#F25E6B,#0[01]E497,#4FADE6$
cra://debug?themeEditor=remove:1
expect-log theme editor pad 4: wheel=complimentary key=#F25E6B,#0[01]E4DB$
# Drab navy goes across the wheel too, kept dark.
cra://debug?themeEditor=swatch:38
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
expect-log theme editor pad 7: wheel=complimentary key=#26456B,#70302B,#606822$
# Page 2: Arc's three analogous colours; − then + keeps the wheel, and from one colour + goes across.
cra://debug?themeEditor=swatch:13
expect-log theme editor pad 8: wheel=analogous key=#F25E6B,#EAAF5A,#F25EC3$
cra://debug?themeEditor=remove:1
expect-log theme editor pad 9: wheel=analogous key=#F25E6B,#EAAF5A$
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
expect-log theme editor pad 10: wheel=analogous key=#F25E6B,#EAAF5A,#F25EC3$
cra://debug?themeEditor=remove:1
cra://debug?themeEditor=remove:1
cra://debug?themeEditor=add:1
expect-log theme editor pad 13: wheel=complimentary key=#F25E6B,#0[01]E4DB$
cra://dismiss
